{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/1406028-on-pre-industrial-demons","id":1406028,"title":"On Pre-Industrial Demons","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-08-02T18:29:40-07:00","id":1406028,"title":"On Pre-Industrial Demons","content":"Have any examples been given on how to portray demons and their powers in pre-industrial cultures? Yes, the Dark ages books give us a number of scenarios, but has any advice been given on how to roleplay a demon in such conditions, with initial Covers and whatnot?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","name":"shkspr1048","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-02T20:09:09-07:00","id":1406044,"title":"","content":"These are incredibly broad questions. Could you narrow the scope with some examples?<br /> <br /> Because right now the only thing I've got for you is &quot;It doesn't matter to God that the radio hasn't been invented yet.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-02T20:23:06-07:00","id":1406047,"title":"","content":"Assuming Satchel has it right (interpreting your question) it does not matter what level of technology humans are on. The Godmachine can make blatantly high tech demons and infrastructure no matter the time (though it should be stressed just as many demons appear organic as appear technical, even in the future)<br /> <br /> And also, demonic powers are completely independent from human tech. It deals with control of reality, not the mere material","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-02T21:37:16-07:00","id":1406055,"title":"","content":"Honestly? Other than certain powers that interact with technology not being available, i wouldn't say anything else actually changes.<br /> <br /> Infastructure is still run by occult physics that defies modern understandings of science, your starter cover fits into the time period and you lack the information you had access to whole connected to the machine. Gadgets after all also defy modern understandings of science so those don't even need to change except some options like software hardware won't be available. <br /> <br /> Pretty much, nothing changes beyond the time period you set it in. If any of your abilities key to a removed skill, see if the embed or exploit fits the new setting and if it does replace the stansard skill with its replacement.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-02T21:53:07-07:00","id":1406061,"title":"","content":"On the demons and angels themselves, it's worth noting that when humanity was still in the hunter-gatherer phase of life, the God-Machine and it's technologies were still hyper-advanced. The heavens were always a thing of the future, and the pinnacle of scientific discovery and technological implementation is holy text and sacred instrumentation. Now considering that this expression of understanding can manifest in making a functioning wooden pan or create a viable piece of infrastructure for utilizing these arcane physics in the form of horse shed, that's not too much of a thing, but it does factor in with the needs for those functions intermixed with the need for secrecy. What this ultiamtely means is that the God-Machine (and the demons who Fell from It) at all time have hyper advanced tech-rail guns na hyrdro lasers nad quantum computing-but that that they hid it as much as possible-but that sometimes these things slipped out. A temple hides wrong right angles that reveal nuclear reactors, but also has infrastructure in the form of gallows that work as seen here, and that demons always have circuitry for their unpublic faces but can also have gadgets that tap into Wi-Fi in the Bronze age.<br /> <br /> For Embeds, Exploits, Demonic Form Abilities, and Gadgets that deal withis, it may mean that some of them aren't AS applicable as they once were, and may be subject to compromise rolls-but they almost never actually live in an era where all of it is useless.<br /> <br /> And finally, where niche occurences matter, hijack the Iron Master's forward thinking principles with the gift of technology and apply powers where it applies even in abstract.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-03T05:21:17-07:00","id":1406091,"title":"","content":"One of the things that I liked in the Pain Prophet's Testament was the underlining concept that the God Machine did not changed as much as humanity has evolved enough to catch up with it- so the God Machine's level of technology was always advanced, and humanity reaches up to try and become like gods themselves. I think that this is more or less the foundation behind the Deva Corporation. Once, humans looked at angels and demons and thought they were divine horrors. Now, they look at the revolving gears and burning engines and tey tell themselves &quot;hey, it is not that unfamiliar&quot;. One day, perhaps, humanity would make its own angels. Maybe they already does so, and the future humanity is the God Machine which sends its own angels back in time in order to make sure that they will create it, and every time that an angel Falls and a mission is lost, the chances of gaining that desired Heaven fail, leading to a future of Hell upon earth. Could be a fun twist for a game, I think.<br /> <br /> However, the thing is that with humanity not being advanced enough, its ability to be used in order to build Infrastructures is also limited by the level of technology availble to it. Ithink that Dark Eras talk about it to some degree. At any case, it only means that the God Machine has an interest in developing humanity, so it will be better used as a tool to serve its goals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-04T11:01:43-07:00","id":1406298,"title":"","content":"This is all very helpful, but I was aiming more for how it would look from a human perspective, or how a demon might try to describe itself,.or the God-Machine's workings, to its cult.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","name":"shkspr1048","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-04T11:50:34-07:00","id":1406308,"title":"","content":"To pre-industrial humans, a lot of it would look futuristic to outright fantastical, depending on how close we are to the industrial era. THere's always gonna be an element of holiness, that what what is seen is an element of the higher divine orders.<br /> <br /> A demon will likely describe itself as a fallen divine agent of the God-Machine or a deviant rebel from the God-Machine, and usually not bother with more detailed explanations because a) Cover matters, and b) a lot of their powers and tools are as intrinsic to them as walking, talking, and breathing are to us. Unless an demon has a high Science score, for most of them trying to explain it is a pointless exercise and a waste of time-even if the human keeps up with the explanation, you have to invent the industrial revolution before you have bouncy castles (and I can reasonably assume the only way this is relevant is if a pre-industrial demon is trying to hasten the oncoming revolution). Most humans might grasp the edges of the explanation depending on the era, but the instance you square the circle, there's a chance you lost them.<br /> <br /> THe God-Machine and their Cults will keep to language of religious cults, because honestly a cultist's direct knowledge is a lot less important than their reverence and obedience.<br /> <br /> A lot of this depends on the context of your era, but basically for the majority of human history, it pays to play to religious, spiritual, occult language most of the time where the scientific language of the day can't keep up, keep the directions simple, and otherwise not share too much. No one needs to know too much in this game of espionage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}